  "display_number": "S21",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S21. Clinical benchmarking of environmental vs behavioural BAA effects.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [
    "BAA differences (years) with 95% CI. Environmental: mutually adjusted (dual-exposure) weighted mixed-model estimates, 1-km buffer. Behavioural: covariate-adjusted linear mixed-effects estimates (N = 3,281 participants; 6,471 observations)."
  ],
  "notes_after": [
    "Behavioural risk-factor estimates were imprecise and included the null; because of differences in exposure scaling, measurement error and confounding structure, these estimates are not quantitatively comparable with the environmental associations (see main text). The environmental rows use the inverse-probability-weighted binary-exposure specification; the per-IQR rows use the prespecified primary (unweighted dual-exposure) specification reported in Supplementary Table S24. EVI, enhanced vegetation index; O₃, ozone; IQR, interquartile range; BMI, body mass index."
  ],
